==Russian==
[[File:LorenzBranchetti BN.jpg|thumb|{{lang|ru|Мужчи́на}}]]

===Etymology===
Attested since the 16th century as {{m|ru|мущи́на}}; the word is still pronounced in a way that is directly rendered by this outdated spelling, but the current spelling more explicitly displays the etymology and the even older Slavic sound structure. From {{inh|ru|orv|*мѫжьщина}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*mǫžьščina}}, from {{af|sla-pro|*mǫžьskъ|*-ina|nocat=1}}, from {{af|sla-pro|*mǫžь|*-ьskъ|nocat=1}}. Equivalent to {{suffix|ru|мужско́й|ина}}. Cognates include {{cog|uk|мужчи́на}}, {{cog|be|мужчы́на}}.

